## Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

### Summary
Vercel Web Analytics is already properly installed and configured in this Nuxt.js project.

### Current Configuration

**Package Installation:**
- `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 is installed in package.json dependencies

**Nuxt Configuration:**
- The module `@vercel/analytics` is added to the modules array in nuxt.config.ts

### Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. ✅ Confirmed framework-specific setup for Nuxt.js:
   - Package is installed via pnpm
   - Module is registered in nuxt.config.ts
3. ✅ Verified no code changes needed - configuration already follows official documentation
4. ✅ Checked git status - no uncommitted changes (clean working tree)

### Configuration Details

According to the official Vercel documentation, for Nuxt.js projects, the setup requires:
1. Installing `@vercel/analytics` package ✅
2. Adding the module to nuxt.config.ts modules array ✅

Both requirements are already met in this project.

### Files Verified
- `nuxt-app/package.json` - Contains `@vercel/analytics": "^2.0.1"` in dependencies
- `nuxt-app/nuxt.config.ts` - Contains `@vercel/analytics` in modules array (line 10)
- `nuxt-app/pnpm-lock.yaml` - Lockfile is up to date with the installed package

### Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel, the analytics will automatically start tracking page views and web vitals. No additional configuration is required. The analytics dashboard will be accessible through the Vercel project dashboard.

### Notes
- The Nuxt module automatically injects the Analytics component into the application
- No manual component imports are needed when using the Nuxt module approach
- Analytics only track on production deployments (not in development mode)
